<title>USA: Delta to cut 600 to 800 jobs in Frankfurt.</title>
<headline>Delta to cut 600 to 800 jobs in Frankfurt.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-01-07</dateline>
<text>
<p>Delta Air Lines Inc said Tuesday it will cut 600 to 800 jobs in Frankfurt, Germany, as part of an overhaul in its Atlantic and intra-European route structure.</p>
<p>The company also said it expects to implement layoffs in St. Petersburg, Bucharest and Warsaw as part of the restructuring.  </p>
<p>Delta's North Atlantic operations now generate about 16 percent of its annual revenues. Delta sees the North Atlantic sector growing to about 20 percent after the restructuring.</p>
<p>Delta's total international operations comprise about 25 percent of its revenues.</p>
<p>For the year ended June 30, 1996, Delta posted $12.4 billion in revenues.</p>
